(footprint "PLR135_T10"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Everlight PLR135/T10 TOSLINK optical receiver. Through-hole, hand-soldered / not JLC-assembled. Origin = pin 1. Body 9.70 x 13.50mm. 3 signal pins (1=Vcc 2=GND 3=Vout) on 2.54mm pitch, drill 0.9 (datasheet phi0.80). 2 mounting posts phi1.15 at 5.08mm spacing, 2.62mm from the signal row. ***The mounting posts sit BETWEEN the signal row and the optical opening.*** Looking from the pin row towards +Y: signal row at Y=0, mounting row at Y=+2.62, body front face (opening) at Y=+11.11; only 2.39mm of body sits behind the signal row. Cross-checked against the Kepler X board (X68k-KeplerX-PCB, U15 x68000-ext:XDCR_PLT133_T10W), which uses the same land pattern. The barrel is meant to overhang the board edge.")
